       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. LLMCOBOL.
      *=============================================================================
      * File:    LLMCOBOL.SQLCBLLE
      * Date:    2026-07-31
      * Purpose: IBM i ILE COBOL program providing an interactive 5250 interface
      *          for querying large language models via the Db2 for i AI SDK.
      *          Supports Ollama and OpenAI-compatible backends. Configuration is
      *          stored per job or as a user-level default. Prompts and responses
      *          are displayed through the LLMDSPF display file.
      *          This program is functionally equivalent to LLMRPG.SQLRPGLE.
      * License: Apache License, Version 2.0
      *          https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
      * Authors: Jack Woehr <jwoehr@softwoehr.com>
      *          IBM Bob (AI pair programmer)
      * Thanks:  Patrick Behr <pbehr@behrbros.com>
      *=============================================================================

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
      *    IBM i ILE COBOL workstation display file.
      *    FILE STATUS provides a 2-byte status after each I/O; byte 1
      *    contains the AID key on a READ from a TRANSACTION file.
           SELECT LLMDSPF
               ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-LLMDSPF-SI
               ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-DSPF-FS1.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Display file FD — single buffer sized to the longest record.
      * File record length is 10280.  All format record layouts live
      * in WORKING-STORAGE; WRITE … FROM / READ … INTO are used so
      * formats never share the FD buffer address.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       FD  LLMDSPF.
       01  LLMDSPF-RECORD          PIC X(10280).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Display file format records — independent WS storage so that
      * moves to one record never corrupt another (unlike FD overlays).
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      *-- RUNSCRN: main run screen
       01  RUNSCRN-REC.
           05  RUN-BKND            PIC X(20).
           05  RUN-URL             PIC X(70).
           05  RUN-MODL            PIC X(70).
           05  DSP-PROMPT          PIC X(500).
           05  RESPONSE            PIC X(500).
      *-- RUNSCRN READ buffer: only the B fields come back on input.
      *-- Output-only (O) fields RUN_BKND/RUN_URL/RUN_MODL are absent.
       01  RUNSCRN-INPUT-REC.
           05  IN-PROMPT           PIC X(500).
           05  IN-RESPONSE         PIC X(500).
      *-- CFGSCRN: backend selector
       01  CFGSCRN-REC.
           05  CURREC              PIC X(10).
           05  CURFLD              PIC X(10).
           05  CFG-BKND            PIC X(20).
      *-- OLLAMACFG: Ollama config sub-screen
       01  OLLAMACFG-REC.
           05  OL-REC              PIC X(10).
           05  OL-FLD              PIC X(10).
           05  OL-PROT             PIC X(10).
           05  OL-SRVRH            PIC X(1000).
           05  OL-SRVR             PIC X(227).
           05  OL-PORT             PIC X(10).
           05  OL-MODLH            PIC X(1000).
           05  OL-MODL             PIC X(227).
      *-- OAICFG: OpenAI-compatible config sub-screen
       01  OAICFG-REC.
           05  OA-REC              PIC X(10).
           05  OA-FLD              PIC X(10).
           05  OA-PROT             PIC X(10).
           05  OA-SRVRH            PIC X(1000).
           05  OA-SRVR             PIC X(60).
           05  OA-PORT             PIC X(10).
           05  OA-MODLH            PIC X(1000).
           05  OA-MODL             PIC X(60).
           05  OA-KEYH             PIC X(60).
           05  OA-KEY              PIC X(60).
           05  OA-PATH             PIC X(60).
      *-- PROMPTSFL subfile record
       01  PROMPTSFL-REC.
           05  P-VALUE             PIC X(1000).
           05  P-SELECT            PIC X(1).
           05  P-TEXT              PIC X(70).
      *-- PROMPTCTL subfile control
       01  PROMPTCTL-REC.
           05  P-RCDNBR            PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
           05  P-FIELD             PIC X(10).
      *-- PROMPTKEYS overlay
       01  PROMPTKEYS-REC.
           05  FILLER              PIC X(1).
      *-- MSGSFL / MSGSFLC
       01  MSGSFL-REC.
           05  MSGKEY              PIC X(4).
           05  PGMNAME             PIC X(10).
       01  MSGSFLC-REC.
           05  PGMNAME             PIC X(10).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Indicator area for DSPF INDARA.
      * WS-INDICATORS-AREA holds 99 PIC 1 Boolean indicators;
      * passed to WRITE/READ FORMAT … INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA.
      * WS-IND-BYTES redefines the same storage as PIC X(99) so that
      * individual indicator bytes can be set/cleared via reference
      * modification: X"F1" = on, X"00" = off.
      * Read indicators back via WS-INDICATOR(n) = B"1" / B"0".
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-INDICATORS-AREA.
           05  WS-INDICATOR        PIC 1 INDICATOR 1
                                   OCCURS 99 TIMES.
       01  WS-IND-BYTES REDEFINES WS-INDICATORS-AREA
                                   PIC X(99).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * FILE STATUS for LLMDSPF — 2 bytes, standard COBOL status.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-DSPF-FS1             PIC X(2).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Exit flag — set when F3 is pressed to leave the main loop.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-EXIT-FLAG            PIC X(1) VALUE "N".
           88  EXIT-REQUESTED      VALUE "Y".

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Global configuration variables
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-BACKEND              PIC X(20) VALUE 'ollama'.
       01  WS-PROTOCOL             PIC X(10).
       01  WS-SERVER               PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-PORT                 PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-PORT-CHAR            PIC X(10).
       01  WS-MODEL                PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-APIKEY               PIC X(8000).
       01  WS-BASEPATH             PIC X(1000).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Subfile work fields
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-RRN1                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Prompt values: single-row fetch target plus storage array.
      * Row-by-row FETCH avoids multi-row host-array precompiler
      * restrictions in ILE COBOL.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-PV-COUNT             PIC S9(9) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       01  WS-PV-FETCH             PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-PV-TABLE.
           05  WS-PV-ENTRY OCCURS 1000 TIMES.
               10  WS-PV-TEXT      PIC X(1000).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Work variables
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-FIRST-TIME           PIC X(1) VALUE 'Y'.
           88  IS-FIRST-TIME       VALUE 'Y'.
       01  WS-INNER-DONE           PIC X(1) VALUE 'N'.
           88  INNER-DONE          VALUE 'Y'.
           88  INNER-NOT-DONE      VALUE 'N'.
       01  WS-SFL-DONE             PIC X(1) VALUE 'N'.
           88  SFL-DONE            VALUE 'Y'.
           88  SFL-NOT-DONE        VALUE 'N'.
       01  WS-RTN-SHORT            PIC X(227).
       01  WS-RTN-LONG             PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-IN-FIELD             PIC X(10).
       01  WS-IN-CURVAL            PIC X(227).
       01  WS-PORT-EDIT            PIC Z(9).
       01  WS-TEXT-LEN             PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-VAL-LEN              PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-LOOP-IDX             PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-MIN-LEN              PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-URL-WORK             PIC X(70).
       01  WS-SERVER-DISP          PIC X(54).
       01  WS-MSG-TEXT             PIC X(80).
       01  WS-SQLCODE-CHAR         PIC X(10).
       01  WS-PGMNAME              PIC X(10) VALUE 'LLMCOBOL'.
       01  WS-STKE-VAL             PIC S9(9) COMP-4.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * QMHSNDPM / QMHRMVPM error area
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-ERROR-DS.
           05  WS-ERR-BYTES-PROV   PIC S9(9) COMP-4 VALUE 16.
           05  WS-ERR-BYTES-AVAIL  PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
           05  WS-ERR-EXCEPTION-ID PIC X(7).

       01  WS-MSGKEY               PIC X(4).
       01  WS-SNDPM-MSGID          PIC X(7)  VALUE 'CPF9898'.
       01  WS-SNDPM-MSGFILE        PIC X(20) VALUE 'QCPFMSG   QSYS'.
       01  WS-SNDPM-MSGTYPE        PIC X(10) VALUE '*INFO'.
      *    Stack entry for QMHSNDPM: program name routes messages to
      *    this program's call stack entry, feeding the MSGSFL subfile.
       01  WS-SNDPM-STKE           PIC X(10) VALUE 'LLMCOBOL'.
       01  WS-SNDPM-STKC           PIC S9(9) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       01  WS-SNDPM-MSGLEN         PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-RMVPM-STKE           PIC X(10) VALUE '*'.
       01  WS-RMVPM-STKC           PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-RMVPM-MSGKEY         PIC X(4)  VALUE '    '.
       01  WS-RMVPM-MSGSEL         PIC X(10) VALUE '*ALL'.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * SQL host variables
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * WS-LLM-RESPONSE: sized to the RESPONSE display field (500).
      * PIC X larger than ~500 causes SQL5044 for CLOB-returning UDFs.
       01  WS-LLM-RESPONSE         PIC X(500).

      * WS-OPT-EMPTY: host variable for options=>'{}' to prevent
      * SQL0206 on '{}' under NAMING(*SYS) in the COBOL precompiler.
       01  WS-OPT-EMPTY            PIC X(2)    VALUE '{}'.
      * WS-BE-OLLAMA / WS-BE-OAICOMP: backend name literals for the
      * backend cursor; avoids SQL0206 on bare token 'ollama'.
       01  WS-BE-OLLAMA            PIC X(6)    VALUE 'ollama'.
       01  WS-BE-OAICOMP           PIC X(17)
                                   VALUE 'openai_compatible'.
      * JSON fragments used by STRING in CALL-LLM.  Storing them in
      * WS avoids LNC0014 "delimiter not correct" errors that occur
      * when double-quote characters appear inside single-quoted
      * literals in the PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       01  WS-JSON-PREFIX          PIC X(26)
                                   VALUE '{"role":"user","content":"'.
       01  WS-JSON-SUFFIX          PIC X(2)    VALUE '"}'.

       01  WS-PROMPT-JSON.
           49  WS-PROMPT-JSON-LEN  PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
           49  WS-PROMPT-JSON-DATA PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-L-PROTOCOL           PIC X(16).
       01  WS-L-SERVER             PIC X(1000).
       01  WS-L-PORT               PIC S9(9) COMP-4.
       01  WS-L-MODEL              PIC X(1000).

      * INCLUDE SQLCA and SET OPTION.
           EXEC SQL
               INCLUDE SQLCA
           END-EXEC.
           EXEC SQL SET OPTION
               COMMIT=*NONE,
               DATFMT=*ISO,
               NAMING=*SYS
           END-EXEC.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
      *==============================================================
      * Mainline entry point.
      * DECLARE CURSOR must be in PROCEDURE DIVISION in ILE COBOL.
      * Placed here, before any OPEN, so the precompiler sees them.
      * They produce no run-time code.
      *==============================================================
       MAIN-PARA.
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE llmcobol_backend CURSOR FOR
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-BE-OLLAMA AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
                   UNION ALL
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-BE-OAICOMP AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE llmcobol_protocol CURSOR FOR
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-PROTOCOL AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE llmcobol_port CURSOR FOR
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-PORT-CHAR AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE llmcobol_server CURSOR FOR
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-SERVER AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL
               DECLARE llmcobol_model CURSOR FOR
                   SELECT CAST(:WS-MODEL AS VARCHAR(1000))
                     FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1
           END-EXEC

           OPEN I-O LLMDSPF
           MOVE WS-PGMNAME TO PGMNAME OF MSGSFL-REC
           MOVE WS-PGMNAME TO PGMNAME OF MSGSFLC-REC

           PERFORM FETCH-CONFIG
           PERFORM SET-FOR-JOB

           PERFORM UNTIL EXIT-REQUESTED
               MOVE WS-BACKEND TO RUN-BKND

               MOVE SPACES     TO WS-URL-WORK
               STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-PROTOCOL)
                      "://"
                   DELIMITED SIZE
                   INTO WS-URL-WORK
               END-STRING
               IF FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SERVER)) > 50
                   MOVE WS-SERVER(1:50)  TO WS-SERVER-DISP
                   STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-URL-WORK)
                          WS-SERVER-DISP
                          "[...]"
                       DELIMITED SIZE
                       INTO WS-URL-WORK
                   END-STRING
               ELSE
                   STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-URL-WORK)
                          FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SERVER)
                       DELIMITED SIZE
                       INTO WS-URL-WORK
                   END-STRING
               END-IF
               MOVE WS-PORT TO WS-STKE-VAL
               MOVE WS-STKE-VAL TO WS-PORT-EDIT
               STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-URL-WORK)
                      ":"
                      FUNCTION TRIM(WS-PORT-EDIT)
                   DELIMITED SIZE
                   INTO WS-URL-WORK
               END-STRING
               MOVE WS-URL-WORK   TO RUN-URL
               MOVE WS-MODEL      TO RUN-MODL

               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM MSGSFLC-REC FORMAT IS "MSGSFLC"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               MOVE SPACES TO DSP-PROMPT
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM RUNSCRN-REC FORMAT IS "RUNSCRN"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               READ LLMDSPF INTO RUNSCRN-INPUT-REC FORMAT IS "RUNSCRN"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               MOVE IN-PROMPT   TO DSP-PROMPT
               MOVE IN-RESPONSE TO RESPONSE
               MOVE 1 TO WS-STKE-VAL
               PERFORM CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES

               EVALUATE TRUE
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(3) = B"1"
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-EXIT-FLAG
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(4) = B"1"
                       PERFORM EDIT-CONFIG
                   WHEN OTHER
                       MOVE SPACES TO WS-MSG-TEXT
                       PERFORM CALL-LLM
               END-EVALUATE
           END-PERFORM

           CLOSE LLMDSPF
           STOP RUN.

      *==============================================================
      * FETCH-CONFIG
      *==============================================================
       FETCH-CONFIG.
           IF WS-BACKEND = "openai_compatible"
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-PROTOCOL =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getprotocol())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-SERVER =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getserver())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-PORT =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getport())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-MODEL =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getmodel())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-APIKEY =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getapikey())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-BASEPATH =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getbasepath())
               END-EXEC
           ELSE
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-PROTOCOL =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getprotocol())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-SERVER =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getserver())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-PORT =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getport())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-MODEL =
                       (VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getmodel())
               END-EXEC
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-APIKEY
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-BASEPATH
           END-IF.

      *==============================================================
      * SET-FOR-JOB
      *==============================================================
       SET-FOR-JOB.
           IF WS-BACKEND = "openai_compatible"
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setprotocolforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-PROTOCOL))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setserverforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-SERVER))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setportforjob(
                       :WS-PORT)
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setmodelforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-MODEL))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setapikeyforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-APIKEY))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setbasepathforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-BASEPATH))
               END-EXEC
           ELSE
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setprotocolforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-PROTOCOL))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setserverforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-SERVER))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setportforjob(
                       :WS-PORT)
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setmodelforjob(
                       TRIM(:WS-MODEL))
               END-EXEC
           END-IF
           MOVE "Job defaults have been set." TO WS-MSG-TEXT
           PERFORM SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE.

      *==============================================================
      * SET-MY-DEFAULTS
      *==============================================================
       SET-MY-DEFAULTS.
           IF WS-BACKEND = "openai_compatible"
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setprotocolforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-PROTOCOL))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setserverforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-SERVER))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setportforme(
                       :WS-PORT)
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setmodelforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-MODEL))
               END-EXEC
               IF WS-APIKEY NOT = "********"
                   EXEC SQL
                       CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setapikeyforme(
                           TRIM(:WS-APIKEY))
                   END-EXEC
               END-IF
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_setbasepathforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-BASEPATH))
               END-EXEC
           ELSE
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setprotocolforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-PROTOCOL))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setserverforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-SERVER))
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setportforme(
                       :WS-PORT)
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   CALL dbsdk_v1.ollama_setmodelforme(
                       TRIM(:WS-MODEL))
               END-EXEC
           END-IF.

      *==============================================================
      * EDIT-CONFIG  -- backend selector screen
      *==============================================================
       EDIT-CONFIG.
           MOVE WS-BACKEND TO CFG-BKND
           MOVE "N" TO WS-INNER-DONE

           PERFORM UNTIL INNER-DONE
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM MSGSFLC-REC FORMAT IS "MSGSFLC"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM CFGSCRN-REC FORMAT IS "CFGSCRN"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               READ LLMDSPF INTO CFGSCRN-REC FORMAT IS "CFGSCRN"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               MOVE 2 TO WS-STKE-VAL
               PERFORM CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(20:1)

               EVALUATE TRUE
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(3) = B"1"
                          OR WS-INDICATOR(12) = B"1"
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(4) = B"1"
                       IF CURFLD = "CFG_BKND"
                           MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(20:1)
                           MOVE "backend"    TO WS-IN-FIELD
                           MOVE CFG-BKND     TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                           PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                           MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO CFG-BKND
                       END-IF

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(6) = B"1"
                       MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(CFG-BKND) TO WS-BACKEND
                       PERFORM FETCH-CONFIG
                       PERFORM SET-MY-DEFAULTS
                       MOVE "User defaults have been updated."
                           TO WS-MSG-TEXT
                       PERFORM SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE

                   WHEN OTHER
                       MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(CFG-BKND) TO WS-BACKEND
                       PERFORM FETCH-CONFIG
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE
                       IF WS-BACKEND = "openai_compatible"
                           PERFORM EDIT-OAI-CONFIG
                       ELSE
                           PERFORM EDIT-OLLAMA-CONFIG
                       END-IF
               END-EVALUATE
           END-PERFORM.

      *==============================================================
      * EDIT-OLLAMA-CONFIG
      *==============================================================
       EDIT-OLLAMA-CONFIG.
           MOVE WS-PROTOCOL  TO OL-PROT
           MOVE WS-SERVER    TO OL-SRVR
           MOVE WS-SERVER    TO OL-SRVRH
           MOVE WS-PORT      TO WS-STKE-VAL
           MOVE WS-STKE-VAL  TO WS-PORT-EDIT
           MOVE WS-PORT-EDIT TO OL-PORT
           MOVE WS-MODEL     TO OL-MODL
           MOVE WS-MODEL     TO OL-MODLH
           MOVE "N" TO WS-INNER-DONE

           PERFORM UNTIL INNER-DONE
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM MSGSFLC-REC FORMAT IS "MSGSFLC"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM OLLAMACFG-REC
                   FORMAT IS "OLLAMACFG"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               READ LLMDSPF INTO OLLAMACFG-REC FORMAT IS "OLLAMACFG"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               MOVE 2 TO WS-STKE-VAL
               PERFORM CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(21:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(22:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(23:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(24:1)

               EVALUATE TRUE
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(12) = B"1"
                             OR WS-INDICATOR(3) = B"1"
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(4) = B"1"
                       EVALUATE OL-FLD
                           WHEN "OL_PROT"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(21:1)
                               MOVE "protocol"   TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OL-PROT      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OL-PROT
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                           WHEN "OL_SRVR"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(22:1)
                               MOVE "server"     TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OL-SRVR      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OL-SRVR
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO OL-SRVRH
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-SERVER
                           WHEN "OL_PORT"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(23:1)
                               MOVE "port"       TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OL-PORT      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OL-PORT
                               MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-RTN-LONG)
                                   TO WS-PORT
                           WHEN "OL_MODL"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(24:1)
                               MOVE "model"      TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OL-MODL      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OL-MODL
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO OL-MODLH
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-MODEL
                       END-EVALUATE

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(6) = B"1"
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(32) = B"1"
                           MOVE OL-SRVR TO OL-SRVRH
                       END-IF
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(34) = B"1"
                           MOVE OL-MODL TO OL-MODLH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE OL-PROT  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                       MOVE OL-SRVRH TO WS-SERVER
                       MOVE OL-MODLH TO WS-MODEL
                       MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(OL-PORT) TO WS-PORT
                       PERFORM SET-MY-DEFAULTS
                       MOVE "User defaults have been updated."
                           TO WS-MSG-TEXT
                       PERFORM SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE

                   WHEN OTHER
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(32) = B"1"
                           MOVE OL-SRVR TO OL-SRVRH
                       END-IF
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(34) = B"1"
                           MOVE OL-MODL TO OL-MODLH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE OL-PROT  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                       MOVE OL-SRVRH TO WS-SERVER
                       MOVE OL-MODLH TO WS-MODEL
                       MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(OL-PORT) TO WS-PORT
                       PERFORM SET-FOR-JOB
               END-EVALUATE
           END-PERFORM.

      *==============================================================
      * EDIT-OAI-CONFIG
      *==============================================================
       EDIT-OAI-CONFIG.
           MOVE WS-PROTOCOL  TO OA-PROT
           MOVE WS-SERVER    TO OA-SRVR
           MOVE WS-SERVER    TO OA-SRVRH
           MOVE WS-PORT      TO WS-STKE-VAL
           MOVE WS-STKE-VAL  TO WS-PORT-EDIT
           MOVE WS-PORT-EDIT TO OA-PORT
           MOVE WS-MODEL     TO OA-MODL
           MOVE WS-MODEL     TO OA-MODLH
           MOVE WS-BASEPATH  TO OA-PATH

           IF FUNCTION TRIM(WS-APIKEY) NOT = SPACES
               MOVE "********"  TO OA-KEY
               MOVE WS-APIKEY   TO OA-KEYH
           ELSE
               MOVE SPACES TO OA-KEY
               MOVE SPACES TO OA-KEYH
           END-IF

           MOVE "N" TO WS-INNER-DONE

           PERFORM UNTIL INNER-DONE
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM MSGSFLC-REC FORMAT IS "MSGSFLC"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM OAICFG-REC FORMAT IS "OAICFG"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               READ LLMDSPF INTO OAICFG-REC FORMAT IS "OAICFG"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               MOVE 2 TO WS-STKE-VAL
               PERFORM CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(21:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(22:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(23:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(24:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(25:1)
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(26:1)

               EVALUATE TRUE
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(12) = B"1"
                             OR WS-INDICATOR(3) = B"1"
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(4) = B"1"
                       EVALUATE OA-FLD
                           WHEN "OA_PROT"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(21:1)
                               MOVE "protocol"   TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OA-PROT      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OA-PROT
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                           WHEN "OA_SRVR"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(22:1)
                               MOVE "server"     TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OA-SRVR      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OA-SRVR
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO OA-SRVRH
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-SERVER
                           WHEN "OA_PORT"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(23:1)
                               MOVE "port"       TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OA-PORT      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OA-PORT
                               MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-RTN-LONG)
                                   TO WS-PORT
                           WHEN "OA_MODL"
                               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(24:1)
                               MOVE "model"      TO WS-IN-FIELD
                               MOVE OA-MODL      TO WS-IN-CURVAL
                               PERFORM PROMPT-FIELD
                               MOVE WS-RTN-SHORT TO OA-MODL
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO OA-MODLH
                               MOVE WS-RTN-LONG  TO WS-MODEL
                       END-EVALUATE

                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(6) = B"1"
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(32) = B"1"
                           MOVE OA-SRVR TO OA-SRVRH
                       END-IF
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(34) = B"1"
                           MOVE OA-MODL TO OA-MODLH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE OA-PROT  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                       MOVE OA-SRVRH TO WS-SERVER
                       MOVE OA-MODLH TO WS-MODEL
                       MOVE OA-PATH  TO WS-BASEPATH
                       IF FUNCTION TRIM(OA-KEY) = "********"
                           MOVE OA-KEYH TO WS-APIKEY
                       ELSE
                           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(OA-KEY) TO WS-APIKEY
                           MOVE WS-APIKEY TO OA-KEYH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(OA-PORT) TO WS-PORT
                       PERFORM SET-MY-DEFAULTS
                       MOVE "User defaults have been updated."
                           TO WS-MSG-TEXT
                       PERFORM SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE

                   WHEN OTHER
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-INNER-DONE
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(32) = B"1"
                           MOVE OA-SRVR TO OA-SRVRH
                       END-IF
                       IF WS-INDICATOR(34) = B"1"
                           MOVE OA-MODL TO OA-MODLH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE OA-PROT  TO WS-PROTOCOL
                       MOVE OA-SRVRH TO WS-SERVER
                       MOVE OA-MODLH TO WS-MODEL
                       MOVE OA-PATH  TO WS-BASEPATH
                       IF FUNCTION TRIM(OA-KEY) = "********"
                           MOVE OA-KEYH TO WS-APIKEY
                       ELSE
                           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(OA-KEY) TO WS-APIKEY
                           MOVE WS-APIKEY TO OA-KEYH
                       END-IF
                       MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(OA-PORT) TO WS-PORT
                       PERFORM SET-FOR-JOB
               END-EVALUATE
           END-PERFORM.

      *==============================================================
      * PROMPT-FIELD
      * Displays a scrollable subfile of valid values.
      * Input:  WS-IN-FIELD, WS-IN-CURVAL
      * Output: WS-RTN-SHORT, WS-RTN-LONG
      *==============================================================
       PROMPT-FIELD.
           EVALUATE WS-IN-FIELD
               WHEN "backend"
                   MOVE WS-IN-CURVAL TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                   MOVE WS-BACKEND   TO WS-RTN-LONG
               WHEN "protocol"
                   MOVE WS-IN-CURVAL  TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                   MOVE WS-PROTOCOL   TO WS-RTN-LONG
               WHEN "port"
                   MOVE WS-IN-CURVAL  TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                   MOVE WS-PORT       TO WS-STKE-VAL
                   MOVE WS-STKE-VAL   TO WS-PORT-EDIT
                   MOVE WS-PORT-EDIT  TO WS-RTN-LONG
               WHEN "server"
                   MOVE WS-IN-CURVAL  TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                   MOVE WS-SERVER     TO WS-RTN-LONG
               WHEN "model"
                   MOVE WS-IN-CURVAL  TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                   MOVE WS-MODEL      TO WS-RTN-LONG
           END-EVALUATE

           MOVE WS-IN-FIELD TO P-FIELD
           PERFORM LOAD-PROMPT-VALUES
           PERFORM CLEAR-SUBFILE
           PERFORM LOAD-SUBFILE

           MOVE "N" TO WS-SFL-DONE
           PERFORM UNTIL SFL-DONE
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM PROMPTKEYS-REC
                   FORMAT IS "PROMPTKEYS"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               READ LLMDSPF INTO PROMPTCTL-REC FORMAT IS "PROMPTCTL"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA

               EVALUATE TRUE
                   WHEN WS-INDICATOR(3) = B"1"
                             OR WS-INDICATOR(12) = B"1"
                       MOVE "Y" TO WS-SFL-DONE

                   WHEN OTHER
                       MOVE 1 TO WS-LOOP-IDX
                       PERFORM UNTIL WS-LOOP-IDX > WS-PV-COUNT
                           READ LLMDSPF INTO PROMPTSFL-REC
                               FORMAT IS "PROMPTSFL"
                               INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
                           IF P-SELECT = "1"
                               MOVE P-TEXT  TO WS-RTN-SHORT
                               MOVE P-VALUE TO WS-RTN-LONG
                               MOVE "Y" TO WS-SFL-DONE
                               MOVE WS-PV-COUNT TO WS-LOOP-IDX
                           END-IF
                           ADD 1 TO WS-LOOP-IDX
                       END-PERFORM
               END-EVALUATE
           END-PERFORM.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * LOAD-PROMPT-VALUES
      * Row-by-row FETCH into WS-PV-FETCH, stored into WS-PV-TEXT(n).
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       LOAD-PROMPT-VALUES.
           MOVE 0 TO WS-PV-COUNT
           EVALUATE WS-IN-FIELD
               WHEN "backend"
                   EXEC SQL OPEN llmcobol_backend END-EXEC
                   PERFORM UNTIL WS-PV-COUNT >= 1000
                                 OR SQLCODE = 100
                       EXEC SQL FETCH llmcobol_backend
                           INTO :WS-PV-FETCH
                       END-EXEC
                       IF SQLCODE = 0
                           ADD 1 TO WS-PV-COUNT
                           MOVE WS-PV-FETCH
                               TO WS-PV-TEXT(WS-PV-COUNT)
                       END-IF
                   END-PERFORM
                   EXEC SQL CLOSE llmcobol_backend END-EXEC
               WHEN "protocol"
                   EXEC SQL OPEN llmcobol_protocol END-EXEC
                   PERFORM UNTIL WS-PV-COUNT >= 1000
                                 OR SQLCODE = 100
                       EXEC SQL FETCH llmcobol_protocol
                           INTO :WS-PV-FETCH
                       END-EXEC
                       IF SQLCODE = 0
                           ADD 1 TO WS-PV-COUNT
                           MOVE WS-PV-FETCH
                               TO WS-PV-TEXT(WS-PV-COUNT)
                       END-IF
                   END-PERFORM
                   EXEC SQL CLOSE llmcobol_protocol END-EXEC
               WHEN "port"
                   EXEC SQL OPEN llmcobol_port END-EXEC
                   PERFORM UNTIL WS-PV-COUNT >= 1000
                                 OR SQLCODE = 100
                       EXEC SQL FETCH llmcobol_port
                           INTO :WS-PV-FETCH
                       END-EXEC
                       IF SQLCODE = 0
                           ADD 1 TO WS-PV-COUNT
                           MOVE WS-PV-FETCH
                               TO WS-PV-TEXT(WS-PV-COUNT)
                       END-IF
                   END-PERFORM
                   EXEC SQL CLOSE llmcobol_port END-EXEC
               WHEN "server"
                   EXEC SQL OPEN llmcobol_server END-EXEC
                   PERFORM UNTIL WS-PV-COUNT >= 1000
                                 OR SQLCODE = 100
                       EXEC SQL FETCH llmcobol_server
                           INTO :WS-PV-FETCH
                       END-EXEC
                       IF SQLCODE = 0
                           ADD 1 TO WS-PV-COUNT
                           MOVE WS-PV-FETCH
                               TO WS-PV-TEXT(WS-PV-COUNT)
                       END-IF
                   END-PERFORM
                   EXEC SQL CLOSE llmcobol_server END-EXEC
               WHEN "model"
                   EXEC SQL OPEN llmcobol_model END-EXEC
                   PERFORM UNTIL WS-PV-COUNT >= 1000
                                 OR SQLCODE = 100
                       EXEC SQL FETCH llmcobol_model
                           INTO :WS-PV-FETCH
                       END-EXEC
                       IF SQLCODE = 0
                           ADD 1 TO WS-PV-COUNT
                           MOVE WS-PV-FETCH
                               TO WS-PV-TEXT(WS-PV-COUNT)
                       END-IF
                   END-PERFORM
                   EXEC SQL CLOSE llmcobol_model END-EXEC
           END-EVALUATE.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * CLEAR-SUBFILE
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       CLEAR-SUBFILE.
           MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(1:1)
           MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(2:1)
           MOVE 0    TO WS-RRN1
           WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM PROMPTCTL-REC FORMAT IS "PROMPTCTL"
               INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
           MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(1:1)
           MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(2:1).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * LOAD-SUBFILE
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       LOAD-SUBFILE.
           IF WS-PV-COUNT > 999
               MOVE 999 TO WS-MIN-LEN
           ELSE
               MOVE WS-PV-COUNT TO WS-MIN-LEN
           END-IF
           MOVE 1 TO WS-LOOP-IDX
           PERFORM UNTIL WS-LOOP-IDX > WS-MIN-LEN
               MOVE SPACES TO PROMPTSFL-REC
               MOVE WS-PV-TEXT(WS-LOOP-IDX) TO P-VALUE
               MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(
                   FUNCTION TRIM(P-VALUE)) TO WS-VAL-LEN
               MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(
                   FUNCTION TRIM(P-TEXT))  TO WS-TEXT-LEN
               IF WS-VAL-LEN > 70 AND WS-TEXT-LEN >= 4
                   MOVE P-VALUE(1:67) TO P-TEXT(1:67)
                   MOVE "..."         TO P-TEXT(68:3)
               ELSE
                   MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(P-VALUE) TO P-TEXT
               END-IF
               MOVE WS-LOOP-IDX TO WS-RRN1
               WRITE LLMDSPF-RECORD FROM PROMPTSFL-REC
                   FORMAT IS "PROMPTSFL"
                   INDICATORS ARE WS-INDICATORS-AREA
               ADD 1 TO WS-LOOP-IDX
           END-PERFORM
           IF WS-PV-COUNT <= 999
               MOVE X"F1" TO WS-IND-BYTES(3:1)
           ELSE
               MOVE X"00" TO WS-IND-BYTES(3:1)
           END-IF
           MOVE 1 TO P-RCDNBR.

      *==============================================================
      * CALL-LLM
      *==============================================================
       CALL-LLM.
           IF WS-BACKEND = "openai_compatible"
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-PROTOCOL = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getprotocol())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-SERVER = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getserver())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-PORT = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getport())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-MODEL = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_getmodel())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-LLM-RESPONSE = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.openai_compatible_chat_generate(
                           TRIM(:DSP-PROMPT),
                           :WS-OPT-EMPTY))
               END-EXEC
           ELSE
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-PROTOCOL = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getprotocol())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-SERVER = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getserver())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-PORT = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getport())
               END-EXEC
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-L-MODEL = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_getmodel())
               END-EXEC
      *        Build the JSON in COBOL into the VARCHAR host variable
      *        WS-PROMPT-JSON.  Setting WS-PROMPT-JSON-LEN to the
      *        trimmed length tells Db2 the exact byte count so
      *        ollama_generate receives a properly-bounded string with
      *        no trailing spaces.
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-PROMPT-JSON-DATA
               STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-JSON-PREFIX)
                          DELIMITED SIZE
                      FUNCTION TRIM(DSP-PROMPT)
                          DELIMITED SIZE
                      FUNCTION TRIM(WS-JSON-SUFFIX)
                          DELIMITED SIZE
                      INTO WS-PROMPT-JSON-DATA
               END-STRING
               MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(
                        FUNCTION TRIM(WS-PROMPT-JSON-DATA))
                   TO WS-PROMPT-JSON-LEN
               EXEC SQL
                   SET :WS-LLM-RESPONSE = (
                       VALUES dbsdk_v1.ollama_generate(
                           :WS-PROMPT-JSON))
               END-EXEC
           END-IF

           MOVE SQLCODE TO WS-SQLCODE-CHAR
           STRING "SC=" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SQLCODE-CHAR)
                  " P=["  FUNCTION TRIM(DSP-PROMPT)  "]"
                  " R=["  FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LLM-RESPONSE)  "]"
               DELIMITED SIZE INTO RESPONSE
           END-STRING.

      *==============================================================
      * SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE  (QMHSNDPM)
      *==============================================================
       SEND-PROGRAM-MESSAGE.
           IF WS-MSG-TEXT = SPACES
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF
           MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MSG-TEXT))
               TO WS-SNDPM-MSGLEN
           IF WS-SNDPM-MSGLEN = 0
               EXIT PARAGRAPH
           END-IF
           CALL "QMHSNDPM" USING
               WS-SNDPM-MSGID
               WS-SNDPM-MSGFILE
               WS-MSG-TEXT
               WS-SNDPM-MSGLEN
               WS-SNDPM-MSGTYPE
               WS-PGMNAME
               WS-SNDPM-STKC
               WS-MSGKEY
               WS-ERROR-DS.

      *==============================================================
      * CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES  (QMHRMVPM)
      * WS-STKE-VAL must be set to the stack entry count before PERFORM.
      *==============================================================
       CLEAR-PROGRAM-MESSAGES.
           MOVE WS-STKE-VAL TO WS-RMVPM-STKC
           CALL "QMHRMVPM" USING
               WS-RMVPM-STKE
               WS-RMVPM-STKC
               WS-RMVPM-MSGKEY
               WS-RMVPM-MSGSEL
               WS-ERROR-DS.
